WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.680
 In our first video, we shared what Project Lit Bronx is and why it's important.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.360
 In this video, you'll learn everything you need to know about how to put on a community

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.280
 book club in 10 easy steps.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.159
 Number one, get the books.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:29.959
 You can secure books through school funds, donations, and donations.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.799
 or crowdfunding sites like DonorsChoose.

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:37.559
 We normally order 30 to 35 books.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.880
 Number two, set the date.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.299
 Once you have the books in hand,

00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:48.479
 choose the date for your book club.

00:00:48.479 --> 00:00:51.120
 We like to give participants about a month

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.579
 to read each book.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.659
 Number three, pass out the books.

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:00.459
 Now, you're ready to.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
 Pass out books to any and all interested students,

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.559
 staff, family, and community members.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.640
 Number four, ask participants to create trivia questions.

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:18.000
 These are questions that can be answered

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.680
 by anyone who's read the book.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.239
 They're usually right there types of questions.

00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:27.500
 Number five, send out reminders.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.200
 As it gets closer to the date,

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.200
 start to remind.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.880
 participants. We like to email everyone who has taken a book, put up flyers

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:41.199
 around the school, and make announcements on our school's PA system.

00:01:41.199 --> 00:01:46.979
 Basketball? Do you love to rhyme? Then the Crossover by Kwame Alexander is the book

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:53.319
 for you. Join us for our next Project Lit Foot Club next Thursday. You can get a

00:01:53.319 --> 00:02:00.760
 copy of The Crossover after school from Ms. Iboza Kinabe or Ms. Al-Dubai.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.320
 Number six, prepare student facilitators.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.760
 We try to make sure that all of our book clubs

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.760
 are facilitated by students.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.800
 So usually a day or two before we meet,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.680
 we gather the facilitators and prepare them for their role.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.479
 This usually means reviewing the agenda

00:02:18.479 --> 00:02:21.440
 and having students decide which parts of the program

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.899
 they want to facilitate.

00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:28.959
 Number seven, prepare all of the needed documents and snacks.

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:30.440
 Now.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.800
 time to prepare everything you need for your book club. Make sure you have a

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:41.159
 sign-in sheet, an agenda for each participant, a discussion guide, a list of

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:47.319
 your 10 trivia questions and answers, trivia answer sheets for teams, trivia

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:53.040
 point trackers for facilitators, prizes for the winning trivia team. These can be

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:59.360
 books, gift cards, you name it, and of course, snacks.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.239
 Number eight, start the book club discussion. Enjoy the small and whole

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:09.560
 group discussion time.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.560
 Good afternoon guys!

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.560
 Happy New Year!

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.560
 So we are three facilitators.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:22.079
 Number nine, wrap it up with trivia and a raffle. After small group and whole

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:27.079
 group discussion, it's time for some fun. The facilitators ask the trivia

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:31.840
 questions and teams race to get there.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:49.040
 answers into the judges number 10 take a picture when all is said and done we

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.879
 always end our project lit book clubs with a group picture to document our

00:03:53.879 --> 00:03:59.760
 experience and share on social media we hope this video was helpful and

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.840
 with you the 10 steps we take to put on a project-lit book club. Our next video

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:12.960
 will focus on how we get the word out to students, staff, family, and community

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:17.000
 members. We hope you enjoy it.
